The map and reduce functions for word count, in the simplified logical form (real Hadoop jobs are written against a Java API with more ceremony):

```python
def map(document_id, text):
    for word in text.split():
        emit(word, 1)

def reduce(word, counts):
    emit(word, sum(counts))
```

Every mapper runs this independently on its chunk of input, with zero awareness of any other mapper. The framework handles everything between `emit` in map and the grouped `counts` list arriving at reduce — sorting, partitioning by key, and shipping data across the network. That's the whole value of the model: the programmer writes two simple functions and never touches a socket.
